+## Sites
+
+A request names its site (kitchen) in the `X-Larder-Site` header, for example
+`X-Larder-Site: annex`. Without the header the site is `main`. A site the
+data does not list is a 400 `unknown_site` error, on every route.
+
+Everything that sits in a location belongs to that location's site, and a
+request only sees its own site: batches and their movements (`/batches`, the
+waste report, `/export/ledger.csv`), stock on hand (`/items`, `/alerts`,
+`/forecast/*`, `/export/stock.csv`), cooking, the stock value report,
+stock-takes and temperature logs. A batch, stock-take or location of another
+site answers like one that does not exist (`unknown_batch`, `not_found`,
+`unknown_location`); an order can only be received into locations of the
+request's site. Items, suppliers, prices, orders, recipes, dishes and the
+outbox are shared by all sites. `POST /jobs/nightly` checks every site.
+
